impl/1123-slice1-env-mount-substrate:docs/DECISIONS.md:294:| **Why** | npm materializes a `file:` *directory* dep as a symlink (like `npm link`), and its `.bin` shim then `realpath`-resolves to the host's global install — outside the workspace root. In direct mode that is fine (the process runs on the host where the link resolves) and is the fastest, lowest-disk option. In a sandbox the target lives outside the bind mount, so the link is invisible/dangling and the realpath guard rejects it; the sandbox must therefore receive an extracted copy, not a link. Unifying both sandbox providers on the same pack→extract path keeps provider-specific code from inventing a separate app-materialization path (see the preprovisioned-base plan's "reuse the serve-time runtime path" constraint). |
