origin/main:docs/issues/391/runtime-refactor/architecture/10-sandbox-deployment-eu.md:242:- **dev tier** is `bwrap` only, trusted/dev/invite-only. It does not satisfy public hostile multi-tenant isolation (shared network namespace, shared kernel/uid/process, no seccomp — the #307 finding).
origin/main:docs/issues/391/runtime-refactor/architecture/10-sandbox-deployment-eu.md:243:- **hardened default is `runsc` systrap on plain EU VMs**, because systrap needs no KVM (so no nested-virt dependency) and matches #307's chosen path. D1 binds its durable local/provider workspace volume; the same host-side boundary remains compatible with X1 later. Egress: per-container netns + nftables (block RFC1918, CGNAT, link-local, metadata, ULA, app/DB networks; allow public DNS/package registries; add proxy/allowlist later).
origin/main:docs/issues/391/runtime-refactor/architecture/10-sandbox-deployment-eu.md:269:- **gVisor `runsc`** and **Kata/Cloud Hypervisor** run OCI images through containerd/Docker-compatible plumbing, so `{ image: { ref, digest } }` is the natural runtime spec for hardened/VM-grade tiers.
origin/main:docs/issues/391/runtime-refactor/architecture/10-sandbox-deployment-eu.md:272:- **`remote-worker` reports image support in its handshake.** The worker may implement OCI-native execution (runsc/Kata) or a bwrap-style unpack path, but the client consumes only reported facts and the resolved digest; missing/unknown support fails closed.
