origin/main:docs/issues/808/runtime-refactor/work/X1-s3-fuse-mounts/TODO.md:50:- **Isolation tiers X1 runs under** (full matrix + providers in `10-sandbox-deployment-eu.md`): **dev** = `bwrap` (trusted/invite-only); **hardened default** = **gVisor `runsc --platform=systrap` on plain EU VMs + per-workspace netns/nftables** (canonical-with #307 — file ops stay host-side, only exec moves into gVisor, host served via gofer); **VM-grade** = **Kata Containers or Cloud Hypervisor + virtiofsd on EU bare metal**, exporting the host rclone mount into the guest **via virtiofs**. **NEVER vanilla Firecracker for live host mounts** — Firecracker lacks generic virtiofs, so it cannot serve the host rclone mount into the guest and would force rclone (and its credentials) into the guest, violating X1 (Firecracker is acceptable only with block images/snapshot/sync, never host rclone bind). The BBX1-003 host-mount-then-bind spec is provider-agnostic across dev/hardened; the VM-grade path swaps the bind for a virtiofs export of the same host mount.
